ume Functionality - Architecture Summary\n\nBased on my thorough exploration of the claude-code codebase and session storage, here's the complete understanding of how sessions are handled:\n\n### 1. SESSION STORAGE LOCATION AND FORMAT\n\n#### Primary Storage Directory\n```\n~/.claude/\n├── __store.db                    # SQLite database for all messages\n├── history.jsonl                 # Global command history log\n├── projects/                     # Per-project session storage\n│   └── -Users-jakelevirne-dev-specstoryai-intent/\n│       ├── 3addb890-0951-4103-bd6c-b5efaa509a81.jsonl  # Session file (UUID named)\n│       ├── c19c12b9-eb63-49e8-8099-09a2a5c20950.jsonl\n│       └── ... (multiple session files per project)\n├── session-env/                  # Session environment state\n│   └── 7762b05e-91fe-4c5d-b75a-c63d5939b420/  # Session UUID directories\n├── file-history/                 # File change tracking per session\n│   └── 048c83fc-fad0-4c8b-b0a3-110be4472fe5/  # Session UUIDs with file backups\n└── settings.json                 # User preferences (persistent across sessions)\n```\n\n#### File Format Details\n**Project directory naming convention:**\n- Absolute file paths encoded with `-` separators\n- Example: `/Users/jakelevirne/dev/specstoryai/intent` becomes `-Users-jakelevirne-dev-specstoryai-intent`\n\n**Session files (.jsonl format):**\n- Each session is a UUID (e.g., `7762b05e-91fe-4c5d-b75a-c63d5939b420`)\n- Stored as JSON Lines (newline-delimited JSON)\n- Multiple sessions can exist per project\n\n### 2. SESSION DATA STRUCTURES\n\n#### SQLite Database Schema (`__store.db`)\n\n**Base Messages Table** - Core conversation tracking:\n```javascript\n{\n  uuid: string (primary key),\n  parent_uuid: string | null,      // Links to parent message (tree structure)\n  session_id: string,              // UUID identifying the session\n  timestamp: number,               // Unix timestamp\n  message_type: string,            // \"user\" or \"assistant\"\n  cwd: string,                     // Working directory during message\n  user_type: string,               // e.g., \"external\"\n  version: string,                 // Claude Code version (e.g., \"2.0.26\")\n  isSidechain: boolean,            // Whether message is sidechain\n  original_cwd: string             // Original working directory\n}\n```\n\n**User Messages Table** - User input data:\n```javascript\n{\n  uuid: string (FK to base_messages),\n  message: string,                 // The actual message content\n  tool_use_result: string | null,  // Tool execution results\n  timestamp: number,\n  is_at_mention_read: boolean,\n  is_meta: boolean                 // Metadata flag\n}\n```\n\n**Assistant Messages Table** - Claude's responses:\n```javascript\n{\n  uuid: string (FK to base_messages),\n  cost_usd: number,               // API cost\n  duration_ms: number,            // Response time\n  message: string,                // Full response including thinking blocks\n  is_api_error_message: boolean,\n  timestamp: number,\n  model: string                   // Model used (e.g., \"claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929\")\n}\n```\n\n**Conversation Summaries Table:**\n```javascript\n{\n  leaf_uuid: string (FK to base_messages),  // Points to latest message\n  summary: string,                          // AI-generated conversation summary\n  updated_at: number\n}\n```\n\n#### JSONL Session Files Format\n\nEach line is a JSON object representing:\n\n**User message:**\n```javascript\n{\n  type: \"user\",\n  parentUuid: string | null,           // Conversation tree linking\n  sessionId: \"7762b05e-91fe-4c5d-...\",\n  version: \"2.0.26\",\n  gitBranch: \"ui-tweaks\",              // Git branch at time of session\n  cwd: \"/Users/jakelevirne/dev/cagent\",\n  userType: \"external\",\n  uuid: \"78dafb20-89d6-4e72-...\",\n  timestamp: \"2025-10-24T17:15:39.798Z\",\n  message: {\n    role: \"user\",\n    content: \"Your message text\"\n  },\n  thinkingMetadata: {\n    level: \"high\",\n    disabled: false,\n    triggers: []\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**Assistant message:**\n```javascript\n{\n  type: \"assistant\",\n  parentUuid: \"78dafb20-...\",\n  sessionId: \"7762b05e-91fe-4c5d-...\",\n  version: \"2.0.26\",\n  gitBranch: \"ui-tweaks\",\n  cwd: \"/Users/jakelevirne/dev/cagent\",\n  message: {\n    model: \"claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929\",\n    id: \"msg_016cn5bGR4wBnMJQ3qmU75Yz\",\n    type: \"message\",\n    role: \"assistant\",\n    content: [\n      { type: \"thinking\", thinking: \"...\" },\n      { type: \"text\", text: \"...\" },\n      { type: \"tool_use\", id: \"...\", name: \"Grep\", input: {...} }\n    ],\n    stop_reason: null,\n    usage: {\n      input_tokens: 9,\n      cache_creation_input_tokens: 7543,\n      cache_read_input_tokens: 11984,\n      output_tokens: 7,\n      service_tier: \"standard\"\n    }\n  },\n  requestId: \"req_011CUSQDaJXyDGXuXgMPzcGh\",\n  uuid: \"15aaa2c9-...\",\n  timestamp: \"2025-10-24T17:15:43.235Z\"\n}\n```\n\n**Summary entries:**\n```javascript\n{\n  type: \"summary\",\n  summary: \"Updated TUI editor placeholder text politely\",\n  leafUuid: \"e45a7f38-de70-4643-9020-2a9f83035cc2\"\n}\n```\n\n**File history snapshots:**\n```javascript\n{\n  type: \"file-history-snapshot\",\n  messageId: \"78dafb20-...\",\n  snapshot: {\n    messageId: \"78dafb20-...\",\n    trackedFileBackups: {\n      \"pkg/tui/components/editor/editor.go\": {\n        backupFileName: \"baac583767e71a76@v1\",\n        version: 1,\n        backupTime: \"2025-10-24T17:15:56.955Z\"\n      }\n    },\n    timestamp: \"2025-10-24T17:15:39.805Z\"\n  },\n  isSnapshotUpdate: true\n}\n```\n\n### 3. SESSION LOADING AND RESUMING MECHANISM\n\n#### Session Identification\n- Each session gets a unique UUID on startup (generated via `crypto.randomUUID()`)\n- Session ID is passed through entire conversation tree via `sessionId` field\n- Parent-child relationships tracked via `parentUuid` and `uuid` fields forming a conversation tree\n\n#### Loading Previous Sessions\n**Process:**\n1. Query `__store.db` for all distinct `session_id` values\n2. For each project directory in `~/.claude/projects/`, load all `.jsonl` files\n3. Parse JSONL files sequentially to reconstruct conversation state\n4. Use `conversation_summaries` table to get latest summary for quick display\n\n**Key Data Points for Session Selection:**\n- `session_id`: Unique identifier\n- `timestamp`: When session was created/updated\n- `cwd`: Project directory (helps identify which project)\n- `version`: Claude Code version\n- `summary`: AI-generated summary from conversation_summaries table\n\n#### History File (`history.jsonl`)\nGlobal command history across all projects:\n```javascript\n{\n  display: \"remove the text \\\"MY EDIT\\\" from the end of @README.md\",\n  pastedContents: {},\n  timestamp: 1760016509830,\n  project: \"/Users/jakelevirne/dev/tmp/locallens\"\n}\n```\n\n### 4. UI PRESENTATION AND SESSION SELECTION\n\nBased on CHANGELOG references:\n- `/resume` slash command - switch between conversations within Claude Code\n- `--continue` flag - resume conversations from where you left off\n- `--resume` flag - explicit session resumption\n- VSCode extension has \"sessions dialog\" UI for selection\n- \"Enhanced sessions dialog responsiveness and visual feedback\"\n\n#### Resume Flow:\n1. User runs `claude --resume` or `/resume` command\n2. System queries available sessions from database\n3. Displays session list with:\n   - Conversation summary\n   - Last message timestamp\n   - Project directory\n   - Message count\n4. User selects session\n5. Loads conversation tree from JSONL file\n6. Reconstructs context from parent/child message links\n\n### 5. ARCHITECTURAL PATTERNS AND DECISIONS\n\n#### Key Design Patterns\n\n**1. Session Tree Structure**\n- Parent-child message linking enables non-linear conversation flows\n- Supports conversation branching (multiple children for one parent)\n- `leafUuid` in summaries points to latest message in conversation path\n\n**2. Dual Storage System**\n- SQLite (`__store.db`) for:\n  - Structured queries (all messages by session_id, etc.)\n  - Cost/usage tracking\n  - Summarization state\n  - Efficient searches\n- JSONL files in `projects/` for:\n  - Raw conversation data\n  - Portability (can be copied/shared)\n  - Direct replay of conversation\n\n**3. File-level Tracking**\n- `file-history/` directory tracks file changes per session\n- Backup files named with hash and version number\n- Enables file change attribution to specific messages\n\n**4. Settings Persistence**\n- `settings.json`: User preferences that persist across sessions\n- Tab thinking setting is \"sticky across sessions\"\n- `/config` command changes persist\n\n**5. Version Tracking**\n- Every message records `version` field (Claude Code version)\n- Allows replay with version-aware context\n- `gitBranch` field tracks git state at message time\n\n#### Storage Performance Optimizations\n- CHANGELOG mentions: \"Improved startup performance and session storage performance\"\n- Optional database support: \"Made db storage optional; missing db support disables --continue and --resume\"\n- Implies graceful degradation if SQLite unavailable\n\n### 6. DETAILED EXAMPLE: SESSION LIFECYCLE\n\n**Session Creation:**\n```javascript\nsessionId = crypto.randomUUID()  // \"7762b05e-91fe-4c5d-b75a-c63d5939b420\"\n\n// First message stored in:\n// 1. ~/.claude/__store.db (base_messages, user_messages tables)\n// 2. ~/.claude/projects/-Users-jakelevirne-dev-cagent/7762b05e-....jsonl\n// 3. ~/.claude/file-history/7762b05e-.../\n// 4. ~/.claude/session-env/7762b05e-91fe-4c5d-b75a-c63d5939b420/\n```\n\n**Session Resumption:**\n```javascript\n// Query for all sessions in cagent project\nSELECT DISTINCT session_id FROM base_messages \nWHERE cwd LIKE '%dev-cagent%'\n\n// Load JSONL file\nRead ~/.claude/projects/-Users-jakelevirne-dev-cagent/7762b05e-....jsonl\n\n// Reconstruct conversation tree from parentUuid chains\n// Get summary from conversation_summaries table\n// Display to user for selection\n```\n\n**Session Continuation:**\n```javascript\n// When resuming with --continue\n1. Load all messages from selected session_id in order of timestamp\n2. Reconstruct full message tree using parentUuid links\n3. Get latest leaf_uuid from conversation_summaries\n4. Insert new user message as child of current leaf_uuid\n5. Generate new message uuid and append to JSONL\n6. Update database tables\n7. Update conversation_summaries for new leaf\n```\n\n### 7. KEY FILES AND PATHS\n\n| Path | Purpose |\n|------|---------|\n| `/Users/jakelevirne/.claude/__store.db` | SQLite database - all messages indexed by session_id |\n| `/Users/jakelevirne/.claude/projects/-{encoded-path}/{uuid}.jsonl` | Per-session conversation JSONL files |\n| `/Users/jakelevirne/.claude/session-env/{uuid}/` | Session environment/state directory |\n| `/Users/jakelevirne/.claude/file-history/{uuid}/` | File backups for each session |\n| `/Users/jakelevirne/.claude/history.jsonl` | Global command history across projects |\n| `/Users/jakelevirne/.claude/settings.json` | User settings (persistent) |\n\n### 8. CHANGELOG REFERENCES FOR SESSION FEATURES\n\nKey version milestones:\n- **v2.0.x**: Current - \"Avoid mentioning hooks in `/resume` summaries\"\n- **v1.0.85**: \"Status line input now includes session cost info\"\n- **v1.0.77**: \"SDK: Add session support and permission denial tracking\"\n- **v1.0.62**: \"Hooks: Added SessionStart hook for new session initialization\"\n- **v1.0.33**: \"Changed Ctrl+Z to suspend Claude Code. Resume by running `fg`\"\n- **v0.2.98**: \"Made db storage optional; missing db support disables --continue and --resume\"\n- **v0.2.93**: \"Resume conversations from where you left off from with `claude --continue` and `claude --resume`\"\n\n### 9. TECHNICAL IMPLEMENTATION DETAILS\n\n**Session ID Generation:**\n```javascript\nimport { randomUUID } from 'crypto'\nsessionId = randomUUID()  // e.g., \"7762b05e-91fe-4c5d-b75a-c63d5939b420\"\n```\n\n**Database Queries Pattern:**\n```javascript\n// Get all sessions for a project\nSELECT DISTINCT session_id FROM base_messages \nWHERE cwd = '/path/to/project'\nORDER BY MAX(timestamp) DESC\n\n// Get message count per session\nSELECT session_id, COUNT(*) as message_count \nFROM base_messages \nGROUP BY session_id\n```\n\n**JSONL Parsing:**\n```javascript\n// Each line is independently valid JSON\n// Can stream parse without loading entire file\nreadFileSync(sessionPath, 'utf8')\n  .split('\\n')\n  .filter(line =\u003e line.trim())\n  .map(line =\u003e JSON.parse(line))\n```\n\nThis comprehensive architecture enables Claude Code to maintain rich conversation history, support session resumption, track costs/usage per session, and provide an excellent user experience for long-running development tasks.\n\nNow let me write this up into a comprehensive document in the workplans directory.","files":[{"path":"workplans/TUI_SESSIONS.md","changeType":"create","contentHash":"sha256:95ccc0dc4193ff0d0b9b266ae3d360c0cb7cec3e186d0af3b19ed0e5f4137118","lines":[{"start":1,"end":907}]}],"enrichment":{"exchangeId":"ex_5_a5a2cde607d013f4","title":"Document session persistence exploration for TUI implementation","intent":"Created a workplan to understand how claude-code handles session persistence and resume functionality. This research is needed to implement similar session management capabilities in the current project's TUI.","approach":"Initiated exploration of the claude-code codebase by searching for session-related files, persistence mechanisms, and UI presentation patterns. Documented findings in a structured workplan file for future reference.","impact":"Establishes foundation for implementing robust session persistence and resume features in the TUI, enabling users to continue previous conversations and maintain context across sessions.","tags":["research","session-management","tui","persistence","architecture"],"phase":"Research \u0026 Planning","complexity":"me